QuestGuidance.Register("en",460,{
[14689]="7000AE55\n1\tDeliver the talons to Emerald Twospade at Hoarhallow\030Collect Wolf-talon (total: 5)\tScattered throughout the Ettenmoors are places prowled by the Darktide wolves. Emerald Twospade believes that the Darktide wolves can be coaxed into attacking the forces of Angmar camped at the Grimwood Lumber-camp. To this end, she has asked you to collect talons from the Darktide wolves.\n2\tPlace the talons on the stump\tThe cut stump is on the outskirts of the Grimwood Lumber-camp. Emerald Twospade directed you to find the cut stump on the outskirts of the Grimwood Lumber Camp. She hopes that placing the talons on the stump will draw Darktide wolves to attack the forces at the camp.\n",
[14690]="7001931B\n1\tWood may be found in the valley of Nen Hilith, south-west of the Elf-camp. Glavrolnen has asked you to bring him several pieces of strong wood.\t\n2\tBring the wood to Glavrolnen in Nen Hilith\tGlavrolnen can be found at the Elf-camp in Nen Hilith, north-east of the wood-piles. Searching through the wood-piles, you were able to identify five good pieces of wood with which a sturdy cask can be built. You should now return to Glavrolnen\n",
[14691]="7001922A\n1\tCollect wood-bundles (total: 5)\tLumber can be found to the south-west of Frerin's Court. Nos Grimsong has asked you to gather lumber for him.\n2\tTalk to Nos Grimsong at Frerin's Court\030Collect Lumber (total: 5)\030Talk to Nos Grimsong\tNos Grimsong is at Frerin's Cour, north-east of where you gathered the lumber. You should return to Nos Grimsong to collect your reward.\n",
[14692]="700529DD\n1\tTalk to Ainhard\tThe forester Ainhard lives south of Vegbár. You should talk to Ainhard. If Ainhard is not at his home, he may have already headed to Vegbár.\n2\tCollect the wood planks\tThe wood planks can be found outside Ainhard's home. You should collect the wood planks.\n3\tRepair damaged walls (total: 10)\tWith the new planks, you can now repair some of the damaged walls in Vegbár. You should repair damaged walls in Vegbár.\n4\tTalk to Skalla\tSkalla can be found in Vegbár, the Beorning outpost in the Wolf-denes. You should talk to Skalla.\n",
[14693]="70046C55\n1\tChop trees on the slope of the Emyn Ernil (total: 10)\tTrees can be found on the slopes of the Emyn Ernil. You should chop down some trees to collect wood.\n2\tTalk to Falastír\tFalastír is located at the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas. You should bring Falastír the wood you gathered on Emyn Ernil.\n",
[14694]="70071B2D\n1\tCollect sarláshi branches (total: 4)\tGôbezhir has asked you to go to Zakhûr in eastern An Shêru to search for branches of sarláshi wood.\n2\tReturn to Jiret-menêsh\tYou have found several branches of sarláshi wood. You should return to Jiret-menêsh so you can give them to Gôbezhir.\n3\tBring the sarláshi branches to Gôbezhir\tYou have found several branches of sarláshi wood. You talk to Gôbezhir and give them to him.\n",
[14695]="7000AC65\n1\tBring the wooden figurines to Maggie Smallwood\030Collect wooden figurines (total: 5)\tMaggie Smallwood is at the Bree Hunting Lodge, west of Bree's South-gate. Maggie Smallwood has asked you to find wooden figurines to sell to travelling merchants.\n",
[14696]="7003A67B\n1\tSpeak with Gifemund\tGifemund is in the ore refinery building near the centre of Woodhurst. The time has come to reclaim the throne of Woodhurst.\n2\tSpeak with Herubrand\tHerubrand is in his hideout in the cellar of the farmhouse in Woodhurst. Herubrand wishes to speak with you after the battle in the mead hall.\n",
[14697]="7002BFAE\n1\tAssist Amal with Demons of the Rushgore\030Assist Frogildi with Survival of the Fittest\030Assist Gisalic with Patching the Contents\030Assist Amal with No Debate\tAmal and his companions, Frogildi and Gisalic, are stranded in the heart of the Rushgore. You should assist Amal and his companions with the tasks they require.\n2\tTalk to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tAmal is at the Woodman camp at the heart of the Rushgore. You should speak with Amal and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[14698]="700359AA\n1\tCraft a long-burning torch for the workers of Wildermore (quantity: see journal)\tHildelith has given you a recipe for a long-burning torch. You should craft a long-burning torch for the survivors of Wildermore who fear the dark and cold.\n2\tDeliver the long-burning torch to Hildelith\tHildelith is in Forlaw. You have crafted a long-burning torch and should now deliver it to Hildelith.\n",
[14699]="7005467B\n1\tListen to conversation of the Orcs along the Northern Wall\030Find a good position from which you might overhear the conversation of the Orcs\tUgrukhôr's forces have been engaged in heated conversation west of Barad Angarth. You should find a good location to listen to the conversation of Ugrukhôr's warriors.\n2\tListen to the conversation of the Orcs along the Southern Wall\030Find a good position from which you might overhear the conversation of the Orcs\tUgrukhôr's forces have had heated conversations west of Barad Angarth, in Zhar Skator. You should find a good location from which you might overhear the conversation of Ugrukhôr's warriors.\n3\tTalk to Dolenthol\tDolenthol will want to hear what you learned from the Orkish conversations.\n",
[14700]="700097E5\n1\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, south-west of Ost Forod, in Evendim. The Ranger Calenglad has sent word that he wishes to speak with you.\n",
[14701]="7003779A\n1\tLook for danger along the road to Aldburg\tAldburg is south-east of Edoras, nestled near the White Mountains. Follow the road that leads to Aldburg and keep an eye out for danger.\n2\tKeep an eye out for additional danger along the road to Aldburg\tAldburg is south-east of Edoras, nestled near the White Mountains. Continue to follow the road that leads to Aldburg and keep an eye out for danger.\n3\tTravel to Aldburg\tAldburg is south-east of Edoras, nestled near the White Mountains. Gandalf ask you to head to Aldburg and deliver the news of Éomer's release and the march upon Isengard.\n4\tTalk to Éothain\tÉothain is at Aldburg in the Eastfold. You should seek out and speak with Éomer's cousin, Éothain.\n5\tTalk to Arcil\tArcil can be found in the Mead Hall of Aldburg. Éothain recommended that you seek out the Thane, Arcil, who has been regent of Aldburg in Éomer's absence.\n",
[14702]="70040A6A\n1\tTravel to Tadrent and speak with Bruidis\tThe village of Tadrent is located in eastern Belfalas, on the south side of the River Ringló. You should speak with Bruidis, the head merchant in Tadrent.\n2\tSpeak with Haelam to learn more about the situation\tHaelam is located near Bruidis in Tadrent. Speak with Haelam to learn more about the Corsair situation.\n3\tSpeak with Bruidis to discuss a plan\tBruidis is located near Haelam in Tadrent. Speak with Bruidis to discuss a plan.\n",
[14703]="7003AB87\n1\tTalk to Éowyn in Edoras\tÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras. Ellen Fremedon has asked you to speak to Éowyn.\n",
[14704]="7003E431\n1\tTalk to Narlinn\tNarlinn is at her encampment, west along the main road from Arrod's camp. Arrod bade you take word of your discovery within the troll-cave to Narlinn.\n",
[14705]="70048C7C\n1\tTalk to Ghai-buri-Sêk\tGhai-buri-Sêk can be found outside the mountain pass in north-east Agarnaith. You should talk to Ghai-buri-Sêk.\n2\tFind Parsâ-dhug-Bhêr\tParsâ-dhug-Bhêr, the chieftain of the Red Sky Clan, can be found in the village Bhol Rûdh. You should find Parsâ-dhug-Bhêr.\n3\tTalk to Parsâ-dhug-Bhêr\tParsâ-dhug-Bhêr, the chieftain of the Red Sky Clan, can be found in the village Bhol Rûdh. You should talk to Parsâ-dhug-Bhêr.\n4\tComplete: Weapons of the Wose\030Complete: A Lost People's History\030Complete: Rally the Warriors\tParsâ-dhug-Bhêr has asked you to help her warriors prepare for the coming battle. You should complete quests in Bhol Rûdh.\n5\tTalk to Parsâ-dhug-Bhêr\tParsâ-dhug-Bhêr can be found in the village Bhol Rûdh. You should talk to Parsâ-dhug-Bhêr.\n",
[14706]="700460AA\n1\tThe High Hall, House of Remedies, and House of Rest are on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Visit the wounded on Torchún's list in the Houses of Healing and see how they are doing. Find Meriadoc the hobbit, Lord Faramir, Lady Éowyn of Rohan, Iorlas, and Echadon in the High Hall. Find Habdir, Bariel, Ormatar, and Thrymm of Rohan in the House of Rest. Find Gísling of Rohan, Ulf of Rohan, and Húndil the Tavern Keep in the House of Remedies.\t\n2\tReturn to Torchún\tYou should return to Torchún, outside the House of Remedies, with news of everyone you visited.\n",
[14707]="7001BA88\n1\tTalk to Anlaf the Forlorn at the Forsaken Inn\tHead south to the border of the Midgewater Marsh and the Lone-lands and seek out the owner of The Forsaken Inn, inform him that the hunters no longer need their rooms. Sam Thistlebur asked that you make your way to The Forsaken Inn to tell the innkeeper that he no longer needs to save their rooms for them.\n",
[14708]="7000178F\n1\tRelay Mincham's concerns to Captain Trotter\tCaptain Trotter leads the people of Trestlebridge, along the Greenway far to the south of the Fields of Fornost. The town lives under constant watch and fear that Orcs of the Tarkrîp tribe will return and complete their massacre and destruction of the town. Mincham's words may sway Captain Trotter to call upon the aid of others from the south. Mincham directed you to explain the true danger of the Orc-tribe facing Captain Trotter and the besieged town of Trestlebridge.\n",
[14709]="7001B1CC\n1\tTalk to Saeradan at his cabin\tSaeradan is at his cabin, south of the Old Greenway Fort. Andreg instructed you to return to Saeradan with news of your success.\n",
[14710]="7006F090\n1\tInspire demoralized soldiers (total: 4)\tShubârza has noticed that the morale of some of soldiers in the camp has been low. She asks that you help inspire them for the coming fight.\n2\tReturn to Shubârza in Amalíbi's camp\tReturn to Shubârza in Amalíbi's camp and let her know you managed to inspire some of the soldiers.\n",
[14711]="7002F019\n1\tBring the wooden figurine to Drafli Broadshield\tDrafli Broadshield is being held captive in a cage partway up the slope of Amon Hen, in the East Wall. Maedal told you to follow the cliff from her position to the south and east until you see the Orc camp. A line of spiked posts lead the way to the camp. Maedal has given you a wooden figurine and a message to give to Drafli to help him through his imprisonment.\n2\tDefeat Orcs on Amon Hen until you find the other wooden figurine\tOrcs and Uruks can be found all over Amon Hen, in the East Wall. Drafli Broadshield wants you to defeat Orcs and Uruks on Amon Hen until you find the other wooden figurine that Maedal was talking about.\n3\tDefeat Orcs on Amon Hen until you find the other wooden figurine\tOrcs and Uruks can be found all over Amon Hen, in the East Wall. Drafli Broadshield wants you to defeat Orcs and Uruks on Amon Hen until you find the other wooden figurine that Maedal was talking about.\n4\tReturn to Drafli Broadshield\tDrafli Broadshield is in a cage on Amon Hen, in the East Wall. You were unable to find any evidence of the existence of another wooden figurine and should return to Drafli.\n5\tReturn to Maedal\tMaedal is on the slope of Amon Hen, in the East Wall. Dafli told you to return to Maedal and let her know that no other figurine could be found.\n",
[14712]="700169C2\n1\tExamine a rune-rock\030Find the rune-rock\tWéorn wants you to find and examine a rune-rock, whatever that is, though he does not know where to find one.\n2\tTalk to Wéorn at the Shadowed Refuge\tWéorn is at the Shadowed Refuge. You should return to Wéorn and tell him of your discovery.\n",
[14713]="70044D59\n1\tTalk to Maenir\tMaenir can be found on the first floor of the Houses of Lore in the Fifth Circle. Mithrandir has expressed great concern about the lost scroll and urges you to speak to Maenir and destroy his transcript before it too falls into the wrong hands.\n2\tBurn the scrawled transcript in the Houses of Lore\tThe fireplace can be found near Maenir in the Houses of Lore. Maenir has urged you to heed Mithrandir's advice and burn the transcript of the scroll.\n3\tTalk to Maenir\tMaenir can be found on the first floor of the Houses of Lore in the Fifth Circle. You have burned the transcript at Maenir's urging and should speak to him again.\n4\tTalk to Gúldil in the Old Archives\tGúldil can be found just inside the Old Archives in the tunnels of the Fifth Circle. Maenir has asked you to seek out Gúldil in the Old Archives as he fears the thief will soon find need of the ancient texts within.\n",
[14714]="70049551\n1\tCollect rations for the Stout-axe smiths in Lûghash (total: 8)\tRations can be found throughout the main level of Lûghash. Freki has asked you to gather rations for the exhausted smiths of Lûghash. You should gather the rations, and then proceed down to the depths of Lûghash to deliver them to the Stout-axe smiths.\n2\tStout-axe smiths can be found on the lower level of Lûghash. You have gathered several rations and should now deliver them to the Stout-axe smiths in Lûghash.\t\n3\tTalk to Freki in Lûghash\tFreki can be found on the main level of Lûghash. You have delivered rations to many of the Stout-axe smiths in Lûghash and should now return to Freki.\n",
[14715]="7003A41C\n1\tCollect pickaxes (total: 4)\tThe new shipment of pickaxes is near the Mine Overseer, near the bottom of Wid Isernore. The Mine Overseer asked you to collect the new shipment of pickaxes.\n2\tThe workers in need of the new pick-axes are near the top of Wid Isernore. The Mine Overseer told you to take the new shipment of pickaxes to the workers in need of replacements.\t\n3\tTalk to the Mine Overseer\tThe Mine Overseer is at the bottom of Wid Isernore for your next task. You should return to the Mine Overseer for your next task.\n4\tCollect ore\tOre has been gathered at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should load the collected ore into the carts.\n5\tOre has been gathered at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should load the collected ore into the carts.\t\n6\tCollect ore\tOre has been gathered at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should load the collected ore into the carts.\n7\tOre has been gathered at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should load the collected ore into the carts.\t\n8\tCollect ore\tOre has been gathered at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should load the collected ore into the carts.\n9\tOre has been gathered at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should load the collected ore into the carts.\t\n10\tTalk to the mine overseer\tThe Mine Overseer is at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should return to the Mine Overseer for your next task.\n11\tRepair the tracks (0/3)\tThe track runs from Wid Isernore towards Woodhurst. The Mine Overseer wants you to repair the track.\n12\tRepair the tracks (1/3)\tThe track runs from Wid Isernore towards Woodhurst. The Mine Overseer wants you to repair the track.\n13\tRepair the tracks (2/3)\tThe track runs from Wid Isernore towards Woodhurst. The Mine Overseer wants you to repair the track.\n14\tTalk to the Mine Overseer\tThe Mine Overseer is at the bottom of Wid Isernore. You should return to the Mine Overseer and inform him that you finished the tasks he assigned to you.\n15\tTalk to Gifemund\tGifemund awaits your return in the ore-refinery building near the centre of Woodhurst. The Mine Overseer instructed you to return to Gifemund.\n",
[14716]="70016BA2\n1\tTalk to Erlar\tErlar is waiting just outside the morroval-workshop, east from the Fanged Pit camp. Hadi asked you to speak to Erlar and help him assault a morroval siege-weapon workshop. Erlar must survive!\n2\tDestroy the morroval siege-weapon\tWith the workshop clear of merrevail, the nearby siege-weapon can be dealt with. Hadi asked you to help Erlar assault a morroval siege-weapon workshop.\n3\tTalk to Hadi at the camp in the Fanged Pit\tHadi as at the Fanged Pit camp, west of the morroval siege-camp. Hadi will want to know that your assault with Erlar was successful.\n",
[14717]="7006BCC1\n1\tDefeat sand-worms (total: 6)\tSand-worms can be found to the TBD Direction of TBD. TBD Lazy Scout has asked you to take over his task of ridding the TBD direction of sand-worms.\n2\tReturn to TBD Lazy Scout\tTBD Lazy Scout can be found to the TBD Direction of TBD. Return to TBD Lazy Scout to inform him you have cleared the TBD Location of as many sand-worms as you could.\n",
[14718]="7000850E\n1\tBring the worm hides back to Rodakhan\030Collect flame-worm hides (total: 10)\tFlame-worms can be found in the south-east part of Malenhad. Rodakhan has asked you to collect flame-worm hides for him and can be found in the camp of Tyrn Lhuig.\n",
[14719]="7000B95D\n1\tDefeat rock-worms of Tâl Bruinen (total: 8)\030Defeat Sarlug\030Look into the distance at the monument west of Cirith Ulunn\tCirith Ulunn, the home of Sarlug, is directly east of Echad Candelleth, but to reach it you will need to climb the sloping path to the north-east, which can be reached by following the Tâl Bruinen road north and east and crossing to the eastern shore of the Bruinen. Directly west of Cirith Ulunn, a monument stands on the edge of the cliffs. Daervellas has asked you to travel to Cirith Ulunn, defeat Sarlug and many of the rock-worms that plague Tâl Bruinen, and to look at the cliff's edge by a monument for Sarlug's mate, Sarnemil.\n",
[14720]="700032BB\n1\tTalk to Dora Brownlock\tDora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet, north-east of Michel Delving. Peony Grubb has asked you to help her friend Dora with the wolves that have taken over her farm.\n",
})
